# Everything in this repository is public: readable on github.com, and served
# verbatim by GitHub Pages while the build source is the branch root.
# Specs and plans reference private repositories by name and describe their
# internals — they live in the private repository kryadov/site-docs instead.
docs/
specs/
plans/

# Build output — generated by build.mjs, published as a Pages artifact
dist/

# Private working files. These sit in the working tree of a public repository,
# so `git add -A` must not be able to sweep them into a commit.
#   private-repos.json  the opaque private-NN -> repository mapping. It lives in
#                       the private site-docs repository now, not here; the rule
#                       stays so that a stray copy can never be committed.
#   private-review.txt  the proofreading dossier for the private copy
#   dist-test/          the build test's output, left behind by a crashed run
private-repos.json
private-review.txt
dist-test/

# Tooling
node_modules/
.idea/

# Scratch for the subagent-driven execution of a plan: ledger, briefs, review
# packages. Generated, disposable, and — like the plans themselves — private.
.superpowers/
